# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-17, C-9). L §6.1 Identities are written: "a place whose kind keeps parts (§3.6) can't be
# stated same at all (LOAD-PARTS), since two members' arrival rules would book its parts"; L §8.3 LOAD-PARTS
# `same <p> = <q>: <x> keeps parts`.
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "8c84b74dc0b49589d87291460bb625f593f0d8ee5d618f9fcce20f9be127f93f"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "b1a051c64f2091b933a1912ca9b1b358dea233fd3267ed1e6c3da2fe98397e48"
  same a.konto = b.konto

ask t: bal(a.konto, 2026-06-30)
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w prorata
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num = 1 at m.day

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-06-30)
